{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall cease.</b> Like חָדֵל לְךָ (II Chronicles 25:16), from doing the thing, and likewise וְשָׁמַרְתָּ (Deuteronomy 17:10). And the meaning: cease, that we leave the thing to him alone; rather, you loosen the straps with him and abandon the load, and it will fall from this side and from that side, and the donkey will stand. And some say: like וַיַּעַזְבוּ יְרוּשָׁלַיִם (Nehemiah 3:5), to load the burden on a distant road."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:34.532197047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}